Customisations applied:
  - Re-authored the agent-style upstreams ("You are the routing agent...", "Use this agent when...",
    "How to Approach Tasks", "Route to a technology agent") into vault umbrella shape: keyword-rich
    CSO description enumerating the five references and the cross-skill boundaries (graylog-log-
    investigation, the metrics skills, EDR/NDR, oncall-runbooks, secrets-hygiene), four-field vault
    frontmatter (name, description, license MIT, metadata.version 1.0.0), skill marker in SKILL.md only.
  - References carry no frontmatter and no skill marker (line 1 is the # Title in each).
  - vahagn openclaw/safety metadata and [Splunk]/[ELK]/[QRadar] inline-label convention dropped;
    methodology genericised, query examples kept as illustrative side-by-side patterns.
  - Two vahagn companion skills merged into a single network-log-forensics.md (with-SIEM and
    without-SIEM tracks), deduped against the umbrella core.
  - Em-dash (U+2014) and en-dash (U+2013) glyphs: zero occurrences across all files. ASCII "->"
    used for pipeline and resolution arrows; commas, colons, and parentheses for dash-style pauses.
  - British/Pacific English applied: normalise, normalisation, prioritise, organise, behaviour,
    licence (noun), defence.

Boundary notes:
  siem-soar-investigation = vendor-neutral SIEM/SOAR strategy, detection engineering, the data
  pipeline, SOAR automation, platform selection, and network-device log forensics. It does NOT own
  Graylog hands-on (graylog-log-investigation, which also holds the Elastic-Stack-as-log-backend
  comparison), metrics-side triage (grafana-dashboards, prometheus-configuration, zabbix-templates-
  and-triage), or sensor operation (endpoint-detection-response, network-detection-response). The
  SIEM/SOAR vendor skills (splunk, sentinel, qradar, chronicle, xsiam, logscale, elastic-security,
  xsoar, splunk-soar, tines, torq, sentinel-playbooks) are skipped/refer-only in this vault per the
  generic-only disposition; this umbrella names them as routing context only.

